        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: bind RunPod release to exact claims",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- bind RunPod destructive operations to exact local claims containing provider id and pod name\n- require explicit `--reclaim` adoption for unclaimed or legacy pods; never silently retarget an existing claim\n- re-read the pod under the release lock and verify both id and name before deletion\n- preserve exact created-pod identity through readiness failure cleanup\n- document the ownership boundary and add the Unreleased changelog entry\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/801\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent candidate: `10e81c43f6b14f53e2005cd6369649f17ce8f62a`\n\nLocal validation on the current candidate:\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/runpod ./internal/cli`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n\nHosted checks are re-running after the rebase onto `origin/main` (`3e82d7fe889e95a804c9846e1b5d9da3edfc6e62`).\n\n## Live gate\n\nBlocked pending RunPod credentials: this shell has no `RUNPOD_API_KEY` or `CRABBOX_RUNPOD_API_KEY`. This PR must remain unmerged until an authenticated create, SSH command, exact-claim stop, and zero-residue inventory check pass on the exact candidate head.",
